, "Notes"],
  Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"LookupAmplitude", "[",
         "taggedParticles", ",", " ", "model", ",", " ", "rightSide", ",",
         " ", "spinIndices", "]"}]], "InlineFormula"], "  ", "Match particle \
names, multiply the stored factor, and relabel typed particle slots."}],
   "Usage"], Cell["Details", "NotesSection"], Cell["taggedParticles has \
entries {particleName, label}; labels may include Multiparticle for a sewn \
internal line. The four-entry spinIndices list supplies the indices used when \
an internal massive state must be explicit.", "Notes"],
  Cell["A lookup of ordinary external particles uses rightSide -> False as \
the third positional argument. The rightSide flag matters for internal-state \
index conventions when sewing opposite sides of a channel.", "Notes"],
  Cell["The matcher handles repeated particle names without replacing scalar \
coefficients, exponents or independent spin-index labels. If a complete \
amplitude is absent, the result is 0.", "Notes"],
  Cell["Use a model containing complete lower-point amplitudes. A product of \
bare vertex tensors is not a stored complete higher-point amplitude.",
   "Notes"], Cell["Examples", "PrimaryExamplesSection"],
  Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["Load HEPCAT", "ExampleSubsection"],
     Cell["Evaluate this setup once before the examples. The paths refer to \
